The following code snippet contains a bug:

```php
    public function __construct()
    {
        parent::__construct();

        $this
            ->files()
            ->name('*.php')
            ->exclude('vendor')
        ;
    }
```

The code fails the following tests:

Test `PhpCsFixer\Tests\FinderTest::testThatFinderFindsDotFilesWhenConfigured`:
            
```php
    public function testThatFinderFindsDotFilesWhenConfigured(): void
    {
        $finder = Finder::create()
            ->in(__DIR__.'/..')
            ->depth(0)
            ->ignoreDotFiles(false)
        ;

        static::assertContains(
            realpath(__DIR__.'/../.php-cs-fixer.dist.php'),
            array_map(
                function (SplFileInfo $file): string {
                    return $file->getRealPath();
                },
                iterator_to_array($finder->getIterator())
            )
        );
    }
```

The error message is:

```
Failed asserting that an array contains '/content/tmp/PHP-CS-Fixer/.php-cs-fixer.dist.php'.
```

Please provide a fixed version of the buggy function, and only that function without additional imports. Make sure the code is between ``` and ```.
```php
    public function __construct()
    {
        parent::__construct();

        $this
            ->files()
            ->name('*.php')
            ->exclude('vendor')
            ->ignoreDotFiles(false)
        ;
    }
```
